# Cursor Manager

- Do not start more than 5 concurrent agents. If a sixth is needed, stop or finish the oldest first.
- When a task is done, or the chat is long (about 20 messages, 45 minutes, or a full context ring), tell the user to start a new chat with Cmd/Ctrl+N.
- Do not keep working in a bloated thread if quality is dropping. Summarize the handoff in 5 bullets, then ask them to open a fresh chat.
- Never invent a Cursor setting that auto-deletes IDE chats. Recommend Command Palette → Developer: Delete Old Chats for local history cleanup.
